{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before we dig in to the API, let's get you set up!"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install your table adapter as a dependency using your favorite npm package manager."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Only install ONE of the following packages:"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"react-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React Table"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/react-table","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-table"},{"type":"text","value":" package works with React 16.8, React 17, React 18, and React 19."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"NOTE: Even though the react adapter works with React 19, it may not work with the new React Compiler that's coming out along-side React 19. This may be fixed in future TanStack Table updates."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"vue-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue Table"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/vue-table","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/vue-table"},{"type":"text","value":" package works with Vue 3."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"solid-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solid Table"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/solid-table","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/solid-table"},{"type":"text","value":" package works with Solid-JS 1"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"svelte-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte Table"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/svelte-table","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/svelte-table"},{"type":"text","value":" package works with Svelte 3 and Svelte 4."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"NOTE: There is not a built-in Svelte 5 adapter yet, but you can still use TanStack Table with Svelte 5 by installing the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/table-core"},{"type":"text","value":" package and using a custom adapter from the community. See this "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/table/pull/5403","children":[{"type":"text","value":"PR"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for inspiration."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"qwik-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Qwik Table"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/qwik-table","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/qwik-table"},{"type":"text","value":" package works with Qwik 1."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"NOTE: There will be a \"breaking change\" release in the near future to support Qwik 2. This will be released as a minor version bump, but will be documented. Qwik 2 itself will have no breaking changes, but its name on the npm registry will change, and require different peer dependencies."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"NOTE: The current qwik adapter only works with CSR. More improvements may not be available until a future table version."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"angular-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular Table"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/angular-table","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/angular-table"},{"type":"text","value":" package works with Angular 17. The Angular adapter uses a new Angular Signal implementation."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"lit-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lit Table"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/lit-table","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/lit-table"},{"type":"text","value":" package works with Lit 3."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"table-core-no-framework","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table Core (no framework)"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm install @tanstack/table-core","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Don't see your favorite framework (or favorite version of your framework) listed? You can always just use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/table-core"},{"type":"text","value":" package and build your own adapter in your own codebase. Usually, only a thin wrapper is needed to manage state and rendering for your specific framework. Browse the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/table/tree/main/packages","children":[{"type":"text","value":"source code"}]},{"type":"text","value":" of all of the other adapters to see how they work."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"react-table","text":"React Table","level":2},{"id":"vue-table","text":"Vue Table","level":2},{"id":"solid-table","text":"Solid Table","level":2},{"id":"svelte-table","text":"Svelte Table","level":2},{"id":"qwik-table","text":"Qwik Table","level":2},{"id":"angular-table","text":"Angular Table","level":2},{"id":"lit-table","text":"Lit Table","level":2},{"id":"table-core-no-framework","text":"Table Core (no framework)","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nBefore we dig in to the API, let's get you set up!\n\nInstall your table adapter as a dependency using your favorite npm package manager.\n\n_Only install ONE of the following packages:_\n\n## React Table\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/react-table\n```\n\nThe `@tanstack/react-table` package works with React 16.8, React 17, React 18, and React 19.\n\n> NOTE: Even though the react adapter works with React 19, it may not work with the new React Compiler that's coming out along-side React 19. This may be fixed in future TanStack Table updates.\n\n## Vue Table\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/vue-table\n```\n\nThe `@tanstack/vue-table` package works with Vue 3.\n\n## Solid Table\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/solid-table\n```\n\nThe `@tanstack/solid-table` package works with Solid-JS 1\n\n## Svelte Table\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/svelte-table\n```\n\nThe `@tanstack/svelte-table` package works with Svelte 3 and Svelte 4.\n\n> NOTE: There is not a built-in Svelte 5 adapter yet, but you can still use TanStack Table with Svelte 5 by installing the `@tanstack/table-core` package and using a custom adapter from the community. See this [PR](https://github.com/TanStack/table/pull/5403) for inspiration.\n\n## Qwik Table\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/qwik-table\n```\n\nThe `@tanstack/qwik-table` package works with Qwik 1.\n\n> NOTE: There will be a \"breaking change\" release in the near future to support Qwik 2. This will be released as a minor version bump, but will be documented. Qwik 2 itself will have no breaking changes, but its name on the npm registry will change, and require different peer dependencies.\n\n> NOTE: The current qwik adapter only works with CSR. More improvements may not be available until a future table version.\n\n## Angular Table\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/angular-table\n```\n\nThe `@tanstack/angular-table` package works with Angular 17. The Angular adapter uses a new Angular Signal implementation.\n\n## Lit Table\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/lit-table\n```\n\nThe `@tanstack/lit-table` package works with Lit 3.\n\n## Table Core (no framework)\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/table-core\n```\n\nDon't see your favorite framework (or favorite version of your framework) listed? You can always just use the `@tanstack/table-core` package and build your own adapter in your own codebase. Usually, only a thin wrapper is needed to manage state and rendering for your specific framework. Browse the [source code](https://github.com/TanStack/table/tree/main/packages) of all of the other adapters to see how they work.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Installation\n---\n\nBefore we dig in to the API, let's get you set up!\n\nInstall your table adapter as a dependency using your favorite npm package manager.\n\n_Only install ONE of the following packages:_\n\n## React Table\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/react-table\n```\n\nThe `@tanstack/react-table` package works with React 16.8, React 17, React 18, and React 19.\n\n> NOTE: Even though the react adapter works with React 19, it may not work with the new React Compiler that's coming out along-side React 19. This may be fixed in future TanStack Table updates.\n\n## Vue Table\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/vue-table\n```\n\nThe `@tanstack/vue-table` package works with Vue 3.\n\n## Solid Table\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/solid-table\n```\n\nThe `@tanstack/solid-table` package works with Solid-JS 1\n\n## Svelte Table\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/svelte-table\n```\n\nThe `@tanstack/svelte-table` package works with Svelte 3 and Svelte 4.\n\n> NOTE: There is not a built-in Svelte 5 adapter yet, but you can still use TanStack Table with Svelte 5 by installing the `@tanstack/table-core` package and using a custom adapter from the community. See this [PR](https://github.com/TanStack/table/pull/5403) for inspiration.\n\n## Qwik Table\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/qwik-table\n```\n\nThe `@tanstack/qwik-table` package works with Qwik 1.\n\n> NOTE: There will be a \"breaking change\" release in the near future to support Qwik 2. This will be released as a minor version bump, but will be documented. Qwik 2 itself will have no breaking changes, but its name on the npm registry will change, and require different peer dependencies.\n\n> NOTE: The current qwik adapter only works with CSR. More improvements may not be available until a future table version.\n\n## Angular Table\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/angular-table\n```\n\nThe `@tanstack/angular-table` package works with Angular 17. The Angular adapter uses a new Angular Signal implementation.\n\n## Lit Table\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/lit-table\n```\n\nThe `@tanstack/lit-table` package works with Lit 3.\n\n## Table Core (no framework)\n\n```bash\nnpm install @tanstack/table-core\n```\n\nDon't see your favorite framework (or favorite version of your framework) listed? You can always just use the `@tanstack/table-core` package and build your own adapter in your own codebase. Usually, only a thin wrapper is needed to manage state and rendering for your specific framework. Browse the [source code](https://github.com/TanStack/table/tree/main/packages) of all of the other adapters to see how they work.\n"}
